# The repo root carries a Python .gitignore whose `lib/` rule (for Python
# distribution directories) silently swallows this project's entire Dart
# source tree. Re-include it here. Do not remove this line: without it
# `git add` reports success and commits nothing under lib/.
!lib/

.dart_tool/
.packages
build/
*.iml
.idea/
.flutter-plugins
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
android/.gradle/
android/local.properties
android/app/debug/
android/app/profile/
android/app/release/
ios/Pods/
ios/.symlinks/
ios/Flutter/Flutter.framework
ios/Flutter/Flutter.podspec
ios/Flutter/Generated.xcconfig
ios/Flutter/flutter_export_environment.sh

# Golden-image diffs, written when a golden test fails. Reproducible from a
# test run; never part of the record.
test/failures/

# THE MAPTILER KEY NEVER ENTERS THE REPOSITORY.
#
# Create maptiler.json beside pubspec.yaml, holding:
#   { "MAPTILER_KEY": "your key" }
# then build with:
#   flutter run --dart-define-from-file=maptiler.json
#
# CI passes the same value from a GitHub Actions secret. A build with neither
# still runs — the map disables itself and says so. See maptiler.example.json.
maptiler.json
*.maptiler.json

# THE SIGNING KEY NEVER ENTERS THE REPOSITORY EITHER.
#
# Without a stable key, every CI build is signed differently and every install
# demands an uninstall first — which wipes the database. With one, updates go
# over the top and the data stays. See RUNNING.md.
android/key.properties
*.jks
*.keystore
